<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    MyOSMC main window: default (fallback) layout.

    Skins can replace this whole file by shipping their own script-myosmc.xml
    in their xml folder (e.g. skin.osmc/xml/script-myosmc.xml). Kodi looks in
    the active skin first and only falls back to this file when it isn't there.

    Contract with service.osmc.settings (see osmc_settings_gui.py):
      controls
        100        centre button: closes MyOSMC (applies settings)
        101..1NN   module slot N-101 (fill order: left, right, top, bottom,
                   top-left, bottom-right, top-right, bottom-left)
        909        Advanced Settings (beta), optional
        9000       optional list/panel container, filled with one ListItem
                   per module (Label, Label2 = description, Icon, Thumb,
                   Property(ID|Slot|FocusIcon|Description)); click launches it
      window properties
        MyOSMC.Count
        MyOSMC.<n>.ID / .Label / .Description / .Icon / .FocusIcon
        MyOSMC.Focused.Label / .Description   (updated as focus moves)

    Every MyOSMC window works this way (script-myosmc-network.xml,
    -appstore, -appstore-info, -services, -remotes, -remotes-test,
    -slideshow). The first-boot walkthrough (walkthru.xml) is deliberately
    left out: it runs before any skin has been chosen. Colours here come from the Home properties
    MyOSMC.Color.<role>; a skin can set MyOSMC.Skin.Color.<role> instead of
    overriding files. The build adds a -720 twin of each file with smaller
    fonts for 720p skins. Details: osmccommon/osmc_skin.py.
-->
<window>
	<defaultcontrol always="true">100</defaultcontrol>
